<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="194" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Email documents (Semantic Search PCF and Document Relationship Viewer): the To/Cc/Bcc side-pane lookup opens above the wizard, not behind it</title>
    <phase>12 Create-wizard lookups and composer (185 dev check fixes)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies shared client code (.ts/.tsx), a PCF control and a code page; tags include pcf.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-frame layering across three hosts (PCF in-page modal, iframe inside a PCF dialog) touching the shared WizardShell modal mode; needs judgment on which surface yields.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>185-fixes</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches DocumentEmailWizard.tsx, which 195 also modifies (summary step). Run 194 and 195 one after the other; 193 is independent.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>pcf, frontend, react, fluent-ui, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Owner 185 dev checks C1/C2 (2026-11-16; notes/task-185-notes.md): in Semantic Search → Email documents and in the Document Relationship Viewer's Email documents, clicking To/Cc/Bcc opens the Dataverse "Lookup Records" pane BEHIND the wizard dialog, so it cannot be used. This is a defect in task 183/188 delivered scope. Owner approved the fix 2026-11-16 ("All three").</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React, Fluent UI v9, Dataverse PCF hosting, Xrm side panes and the @spaarke/ui-components WizardShell/SprkModal layering.</role>
  <goal>In both hosts the recipient lookup opens visibly above the Email documents wizard, the pick lands as a chip, Cancel keeps earlier picks, and the wizard returns to its normal layer afterwards — using the existing yield-to-side-pane mechanism, not a new one.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>
- Semantic Search PCF: DocumentEmailWizard is not embedded, so WizardShell.tsx ~548-560 wraps it in a blocking SprkModal (`modalType='modal'`) and passes neither `nonBlocking` nor `yieldToSidePane`. The composer's recipient lookup goes through `createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.onLookupRecipients` (called from SendEmailFollowOnStep.tsx ~385) → `Xrm.Utility.lookupObjects`. A PCF renders in the Dataverse page's own document, so the Fluent dialog layer sits over the lookup pane.
- Reference that works: SendEmailDialog.tsx ~314-361 `wrapLookup` with `yieldToSidePane` lowers its modal under the pane via SprkModal/sidePaneLayering.ts, then restores it. Copy that; do not write a second layering mechanism.
- Hosts that already work (Create Project code page, Console) run inside an iframe, so the pane opens in the top window above the whole iframe.
- Document Relationship Viewer: Semantic Search's Find Similar opens it as an in-page iframe inside the PCF's own FindSimilarViewerDialog (SemanticSearchControl.tsx ~731-736; FindSimilarViewerDialog.tsx). Its lookup opens in the top window, underneath that OUTER dialog, so fixing the inner wizard is not enough: the outer dialog must yield (postMessage from the iframe to the PCF, reusing sidePaneLayering) or the viewer must open as a top-level `Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo` dialog. Choose the option that changes the least behaviour and record why in the task notes. Also check the DRV opened directly from a form (not via Semantic Search) still works.
- Line numbers are at origin/master `ce6c241964`; re-grep before editing.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/Wizard/WizardShell.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/DocumentEmailWizard.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WizardFollowOns/steps/SendEmailFollowOnStep.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/FindSimilarViewer/FindSimilarViewerDialog.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/pcf/SemanticSearchControl/SemanticSearchControl/SemanticSearchControl.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/wrappers/SendEmailDialog.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkModal/sidePaneLayering.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner directive 2026-11-12, applies to every file this task touches: reuse the existing side-pane lookup and the existing EmailComposer; never re-create either. Reuse sidePaneLayering/yieldToSidePane; no second layering mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">A WizardShell change is opt-in: every WizardShell host other than the two in this task renders and layers exactly as today (embedded mode untouched; existing WizardShell tests unchanged and passing).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-006 / ADR-022">The PCF keeps its platform React; follow docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md (version bump in every location; `npm run build:prod`; judge the build by its output, pcf-scripts exits 0 on failure).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Every UI change in this task uses Fluent v9 and semantic tokens only; light and dark both fully themed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No deploy in this task. The dev deploy of the PCF and the DRV code page is a separate owner-approved step from master (D-126), scoped publish only.</constraint>
  </constraints>
